@startuml
title Plate - User Creates Workout Post Activity Diagram



|User|
:Open Plate app;
:Select "Create Workout Post";
:Enter workout details;

note right
Workout title
Workout type
Duration
Exercises
Sets
Reps
Weight
Notes
Caption
Visibility
end note

:Submit workout post;

|Frontend / PWA|
:Validate workout form;

if (Form data valid?) then (Yes)
  :Send workout data to Fitness Logging Service;
else (No)
  :Show validation errors;
  stop
endif

|Fitness Logging Service|
:Receive workout request;
:Validate workout payload;
:Validate user_id and tenant_id references;

if (User and tenant references valid?) then (Yes)
  :Create workout record;
  :Create exercise records;
  :Create workout set records;
else (No)
  |Frontend / PWA|
  :Show invalid user or tenant error;
  stop
endif

|Fitness Logging Service|
:Return workout_id to Frontend;

|Frontend / PWA|
:Send post creation request to Social Feed Service;

note right
Includes:
workout_id
user_id
tenant_id
caption
visibility
post_type = WORKOUT
end note

|Social Feed Service|
:Receive post creation request;
:Validate post payload;
:Create post record;
:Attach workout reference to post;

if (Post visibility is public or followers only?) then (Yes)
  :Make post available in feed;
else (Private)
  :Save post to user's private profile feed only;
endif

|Social Feed Service|
:Return created post;

|Frontend / PWA|
:Show success message;
:Redirect user to created workout post;

|User|
:Views workout post on profile feed;

stop

@enduml